 how much energy should be produced by each generator on the grid giv~~
en constraints on branch capacity, generation capability, demand leve~~
l at each node, and cost per kWh of generation for each generator.   ~~
The network is solved using a linear program that minimized generatio~~
n cost.~
~
The model assumes the impedance for each branch is purely imaginary (~~
i.e., no resistive real-part), and that all nodes are at the same AC ~~
voltage (only the phase varies).Author: Lonnie Chrisman, Ph.D.~
Lumina Decison SystemsDate: Tue, Jul 22, 2008 9:35 AMSaveauthor: LonnieSavedate: Tue, Jul 22, 2008 3:34 PMDefaultsize: 48,24Diagstate: 1,1,7,1052,484,17Windstate: 2,442,422,476,361Fontstyle: Arial, 15Fileinfo: 0,Model Electrical_transmiss,2,2,0,0,W:\TestModels\Electrica~~
l Transmission.ANAVariable YTitle: Admittance matrixUnits: imaginary mhosDescription: The admittance matrix for all transmission lines (a squar~~
e matrix on Node x Node2).Definition: var adm := Branch_definition[Branch_info='Admittance'];~
var y1 := sum(if to_node=Node and from_node=Node2 then adm else 0,Bra~~
nch);~
var y2 := transpose(y1,node,node2) + y1;~
-y2 + sum(y2,Node2) * (node=node2)Nodelocation: 280,264,1Nodesize: 52,24Windstate: 2,493,319,476,224Defnstate: 2,49,437,677,272,0,MIDMValuestate: 2,52,71,652,284,0,MIDMReformdef: [Node2,Node]Reformval: [Node2,Node]Decision Branch_definitionTitle: Branch DefinitionDescription: Defines the branches (i.e., transmission lines) that exis~~
t in the network.  Each branch connects two nodes and has an impedanc~~
e and a maximum power capacity.~
~
The direction of the branch determines the sign of the branch flow in~~
 the results.  A postive branch flow means that power flows from the ~~
"From" node to the "To" node.  A negative flow indicates power transf~~
er in the opposite direction.Definition: Table(Branch_info,Branch)(~
1,1,1,2,2,2,3,3,3,4,4,6,7,~
2,5,7,3,5,6,4,6,8,5,7,8,8,~
20,20,14,15,25,18,40,21,10,20,30,35,45,~
1M,500K,500K,300K,1.5M,500K,2M,100K,300K,1.5M,400K,1M,2M~
)Nodelocation: 88,264,1Nodesize: 56,24Windstate: 2,227,340,476,224Defnstate: 2,464,80,416,461,0,MIDMAliases: Formnode Transmission_lines1Reformdef: [Branch_info,Branch]Reformval: [Branch_info,Branch]Variable ZTitle: Reactance matrixUnits: imaginary ohmsDescription: Square Reactance matrix (Node x Node2) for all branches. ~~
 Assumed that the resistive (real part) of the impedance is zero for ~~
all branches.Definition: var nonRef[node] := node<>Reference_node;~
index n := subset( nonRef );~
index n2 := n;~
var yy := y[node=n,node2=n2];~
var zz := Invert(yy,n,n2);~
if node=Reference_node or node2=Reference_node then 0 else zz[n=node,~~
n2=node2]~
Nodelocation: 424,264,1Nodesize: 48,24Valuestate: 2,30,58,517,281,0,MIDMReformval: [Node2,Node]Numberformat: 2,F,2,2,0,0,2,0,$,0,"ABBREV",0Variable Shift_factorsTitle: Shift FactorsDefinition: var ybr := if Branch_definition[Branch_info='To']=Node the~~
n Branch_definition[Branch_info='Admittance']~
         else if Branch_definition[Branch_info='From']=Node then -Bra~~
nch_definition[Branch_info='Admittance']~
         else 0;~
sum(ybr[node=node2] * Z,node2)Nodelocation: 552,264,1Nodesize: 48,24Valuestate: 2,395,23,600,328,0,MIDMReformval: [Node,Branch]Numberformat: 2,F,2,2,0,0,2,0,$,0,"ABBREV",0{!40000|Att_resultslicestate: [Voltage,1,Branch,1,Node,1]}Variable From_nodeTitle: From nodeDefinition: Branch_definition[Branch_info='From']Nodelocation: 64,296,2Nodesize: 36,8Nodeinfo: 1,1,1,1,1,1,1,,0,Nodefont: Arial, 10Variable To_nodeTitle: To nodeDefinition: Branch_definition[Branch_info='To']Nodelocation: 120,296,1Nodesize: 36,8Nodeinfo: 1,1,1,1,1,1,1,,0,Nodefont: Arial, 10Chance DemandTitle: DemandUnits: WattsDescription: Consumer power demand to be met at each node.  ~
